  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the Shiba Inu dog as the carrier of the hateful sentiment",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the Shiba Inu dog, which is visually mapped as the entity expressing the hateful sentiment 'i do not like black people'. This projection is implicit, as the meme uses the dog's innocent and indifferent expression as an analogical anchor to represent the sentiment, thereby encouraging the viewer to project their own identity or attitude onto the dog as if it were the source of the message. The dog becomes the visual vessel for the user's projected hateful sentiment, even though the dog is incapable of such feelings. This is a form of analogical mapping where the user's internal state or attitude is projected onto the visual material.",
